# Official openOODA Scripts

All board automation lives in `openOODA/scripts/` (`*.oo` — native openOODA). Product smokes and builders live in `ooda/scripts/`.

**Kept `.oot` files:** Board keeps only `openOODA/*.oot` (BOOTSTRAP, DESIGN, PM, SPRINT, RULES, OODA, SWARM, PROBE, SCRIPTS, CAPS, README + `RFC-*.oot` + `audit/*.oot` + `bootstrap/*.oot` + `rfcs/*.oot`). Research keeps `docs/research/**/*.oot` (`RP-*.oot`, `DOC-*.oot`, `TEMPLATE.oot`, `CONFLICTS.oot`). Brand `brand/DESIGN_SYSTEM.oot` and GitHub `bug_report/feature_request` are also kept. `scratch/*.oot` is debris and is not kept.

## Active Scripts — `openOODA/scripts/` (renamed to match what they do)

- **`check_board.oo`** (was `check_oot.oo`) — In plain English: keep only approved `openOODA/*.oot` boards. Checks `openOODA/` only; `audit/` and `docs/research/` are out of scope. Deletes any other `.oot` debris. Fails closed.
- **`verify_all.oo`** (was `check_all.oo`) — In plain English: run `oodac check` on every `.oo` file and report how many passed or failed.
- **`filter_failures.oo`** (was `check_61.oo`) — In plain English: show the failed files for an issue. Pass the log file as an argument; falls back to `audit/current_failures.log`. Personal hard path removed.
- **`purge_audit.oo`** (was `audit_clean.oo`) — In plain English: delete Python/C debris (`*.py, *.c, *.o, *.log`) left in `audit/` by helpers. Keeps `.oot` logs.

> `ooda/scripts/ci_product.sh` and `*_smoke.sh` are product smokes, not board scripts. They live in `ooda/scripts/`.
> Goal: rewrite bash smokes as `.oo` over time **[STATUS: residual — bash smokes still in use]**.
